teach.description:
{frame_image}

Type the meter's reading, every drum from left to right, for example `{example}`. Drums left of the crop count too: type them as the meter shows them, and the reading follows them from then on. Decimal drums right of the crop may be typed as well; they are left out. Read the drums, not the outlines: a drum between two digits counts as the lower one. Each drum of the crop showing a whole digit is learnt.

Digits learnt: {known}. Still to learn: {unknown}. Teach again later, when the meter shows other digits, to learn them sooner; the meter also learns them on its own as it turns.

